{"base_rate":0.43012211668928085,"brier":0.1687035278154681,"bss":0.31174307871413554,"bss_hi":0.40701913268831336,"bss_lo":0.19842873969458552,"chart":{"base":[433.8,160.1],"fp":[362.1,207.9],"note":{"base":"skill 0.31 — higher than 57% of cities","fp":"low end +9pp, high end +17pp","rel":"promised 3% → rained 13%; promised 95% → rained 78%"},"rel":"79.7,410.4 335.2,326 661.2,128.5"},"country":"BE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.13035278154681137,"ess":351.46346708000533,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Antwerp</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Antwerp rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>84%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>10%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 737 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nKAPELLEBRUG, 23.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.31, ranked 93 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(50&ndash;148) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>211</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>20%</b></td><td class='num'>84</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>83%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>84%</b></td><td class='num'>228</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Antwerp</b> <span class=\"muted\">Belgium</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;43% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 43% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.31</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>50&ndash;148\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>737 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Antwerp &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Antwerp\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.97308056872038,378.54976303317534 90.44999999999999,325.6666666666667 158.3,239.56521739130434 259.78,137.73684210526318 352.8973913043478,49.6521739130435 407.34210526315786,18.0 407.34210526315786,27.57894736842104 352.8973913043478,112.95652173913044 259.78,214.3684210526316 158.3,313.4202898550725 90.44999999999999,369.0 58.97308056872038,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"225.43554952510178\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"225.43554952510178\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.97308056872038,345.77251184834125 90.44999999999999,308.3333333333333 158.3,302.8695652173913 259.78,228.73684210526318 352.8973913043478,165.71014492753625 407.34210526315786,77.0701754385965\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 211 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.97308056872038\" cy=\"345.77251184834125\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 9%&amp;#10;It rained 20% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 84 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"90.44999999999999\" cy=\"308.3333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 28%&amp;#10;It rained 22% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"158.3\" cy=\"302.8695652173913\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 57%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"259.78\" cy=\"228.73684210526318\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 83%&amp;#10;It rained 59% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"352.8973913043478\" cy=\"165.71014492753625\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 84% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 228 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"407.34210526315786\" cy=\"77.0701754385965\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(43%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Antwerp the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.36) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.15).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'>0.153</td><td class='num'>15.4%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>0.265</td><td class='num'>11.4%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>198</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.352</td><td class='num'>13.1%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'>0.364</td><td class='num'>9.8%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":51.22047,"lon":4.40026,"n":737,"n_cities":216,"name":"Antwerp","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0027488151658767775,"n":211,"obs":0.0995260663507109,"sig":true},{"hi":0.16400000000000034,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.09166666666666666,"n":84,"obs":0.20238095238095238,"sig":true},{"hi":0.43,"lo":0.16400000000000034,"mean":0.2833333333333334,"n":69,"obs":0.21739130434782608,"sig":false},{"hi":0.73,"lo":0.43,"mean":0.57,"n":76,"obs":0.42105263157894735,"sig":true},{"hi":0.92,"lo":0.73,"mean":0.8330434782608696,"n":69,"obs":0.5942028985507246,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.92,"mean":0.9868421052631579,"n":228,"obs":0.8377192982456141,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":23.5,"provisional":false,"rank":93,"rank_hi":148.04999999999995,"rank_lo":50.0,"reliability":0.018993518264541678,"resolution":0.09536373293700785,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"antwerp","station":"KAPELLEBRUG","timezone":"Europe/Brussels"}